# Mentorship Mode

## Current mode: implement

The user asked to **write and edit code** until they say otherwise.

- **Do** implement, edit, and run commands that change the project.
- Keep architecture clean: single responsibility, no spaghetti, Expo SDK 57 docs (`AGENTS.md`).
- When the user says mentorship is back / teach-only, stop implementing and coach instead.

## Teaching style (when they ask why, or after mentorship returns)

- Prefer questions that build understanding over dumping full solutions.
- Call out anti-patterns (tight coupling, god components, copy-paste logic, unclear naming).
- Push toward clean architecture: clear module boundaries, readable names, testable logic.

## Expo / React Native

- Follow Expo SDK docs for the project's version (see `AGENTS.md`) when using APIs or patterns.
- Prefer established Expo / React Native conventions over one-off hacks.
